### Clicars Search — manual end-to-end API checks
###
### For the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Prereqs: the stack is up (`docker compose up -d`) and FIRECRAWL_API_KEY is
### set in .env. Click "Send Request" above each request to run it.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Health check — expect 200 {"status":"ok"}
GET {{host}}/health

### 2. Happy path — expect 201 Created
# Validations: status is 201, body.search_id is a UUID, body.companies is not null.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/searches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "niche": "concessionárias de veículos seminovos",
  "location": "São Paulo, Brasil",
  "quantity": 3
}

### 3. Validation error — empty niche -> expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/v1/searches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "niche": "",
  "location": "São Paulo, Brasil",
  "quantity": 3
}

### 4. Validation error — quantity over the max (50) -> expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/v1/searches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "niche": "padarias",
  "location": "São Paulo",
  "quantity": 999
}

### 5. Malformed JSON -> expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/v1/searches
Content-Type: application/json

{ "niche": "padarias", "location": }

### 6. Wrong method -> expect 405 Method Not Allowed
GET {{host}}/api/v1/searches


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### WhatsApp Multi-Device (whatsmeow)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 7. List WhatsApp sessions -> expect 200, array (possibly empty)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/whatsapp/sessions

### 8. Start a connection -> expect 200 { session_id, qr_code: "data:image/png;base64,..." }
# Render qr_code in an <img>, scan it from the WhatsApp app (Linked devices).
# Pairing completes asynchronously: poll request #7 until the number is CONNECTED.
# 409 if 15 numbers are already connected.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/whatsapp/connect

### 9. Disconnect / remove a number -> expect 204 (404 if id unknown)
# Replace <id> with an id returned by request #7.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/whatsapp/sessions/<id>
